window.docContents[205].resolve({"/part-3-internal/ch12-internal-functions/#ch12-internal-functions":{"contents":"Just as sequences of subsets (A_n) assemble internal sets, sequences of partial real functions (f_n : A_n \\to \\mathbb{R}) assemble internal functions [f_n] : [A_n] \\to \\mathbb{R}^* in Ch12_InternalFunctions.lean (1,679 lines).\n\nThe superstar class of internal sets is the hyperfinite sets: internal sets A = [A_n] arising from sequences of finite sets A_n \\subseteq \\mathbb{R}. Even though a hyperfinite set with unlimited internal cardinality |A| = [|A_n|] = N \\in \\mathbb{N}^*_\\infty is uncountably infinite from the outside, from the inside it behaves exactly like a finite set:\n\n* Every nonempty hyperfinite subset of \\mathbb{R}^* attains an exact maximum and minimum element!* Hyperfinite Pigeonhole Principle: No internal injection can map a hyperfinite set A into a proper internal subset B \\subsetneq A!* Hyperfinite Summation (hypersum): Any internal function F can be summed over any hyperfinite set S = [S_n] via \\sum_{x \\in S} F(x) := \\bigl[\\sum_{x \\in S_n} f_n(x)\\bigr], obeying linearity, monotonicity, and disjoint-union additivity—providing the exact foundation for hyperfinite Riemann integration (Ch. 9) and Loeb probability spaces (Ch. 16).\n\nsection\nopen Goldblatt\n\n-- Hyperfinite summation linearity, disjoint additivity, and step partitions:\n#check @hypersum_add\n#check @hypersum_union_disjoint\n#check @hypersum_mono\n#check @hyperStepPartition_eq_and_hypercard\nend\n\n\n","context":"Lectures on the Hyperreals — Interactive Lean 4 & Spatial Edition\u0009Part III — Internal & External Entities","header":"3.2. Chapter 12: Internal Functions, Hyperfinite Sets & Pigeonhole","id":"/part-3-internal/ch12-internal-functions/#ch12-internal-functions"}});